# Master item table for Item Hunt (auto-generated).
# 1-indexed: list[0] is a placeholder so the random number N maps to list[N].
# Items are grouped by dimension tier so the dimension config can pick a range:
#   Overworld : indices 1..1046
#   Nether    : indices 1047..1182  (Overworld + Nether)
#   End       : indices 1183..1218  (Overworld + Nether + End)
# The dimension option is cumulative: nether range includes overworld, end includes all.
# 1218 items total (indices 1..1218).
#
# Every item here is obtainable in vanilla survival. Deliberately absent:
# creative-only blocks (bedrock, barrier, spawner, budding_amethyst, command_block,
# structure_block, light, debug_stick, end_portal_frame, farmland, dirt_path,
# petrified_oak_slab, suspicious_sand/gravel, reinforced_deepslate, player_head,
# spawn eggs), plus these, which look obtainable but are not:
#   frogspawn      - empty loot table, drops nothing even with Silk Touch
#   chorus_plant   - its loot table drops chorus_fruit, never the block
#   infested_*     - the Silk Touch entry returns the clean block (stone), x7
#   bundle         - in 1.21.1 the recipe only exists in the experimental
#                    "bundle" feature datapack, so survival cannot reach it
#
# Tier placement follows what the item COSTS, not where it is found:
# daylight_detector and observer need nether quartz, and skull_banner_pattern
# needs a wither skeleton skull, so all three sit in the Nether tier even
# though you use them in the Overworld.

data modify storage item_hunt:items list set value [{id:"",name:""}]
